# EAS Build archive exclusions (repository root).
#
# EAS uploads the whole git repository, so anything not listed here is packed
# into the build archive. The repository carries a lot that the Android/iOS
# app build has no use for - the mechanical enclosure CAD, the PocketBase
# binaries, the ESP32 firmware build output and the legacy trees - which made
# the archive ~3 GB and the build slow and fragile.
#
# The app build only needs the Expo project itself (frontend/mobile_app), the
# landing page, and the shared config at the root. The `**/` prefix matters:
# the heavy trees live under v3-mqtt-pocketbase/, not at the root.

.git/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.expo/
**/android/
**/ios/
**/*.log
**/*.tgz
**/*.tar.gz

# Transient deploy staging (the deploy script now stages outside the repo).
.deploy-stage/

# Not needed to build the app.
**/enclosure/
**/builds/
**/deploy/
**/firmware/
**/legacy/
**/youtube/
**/downloads/
**/training_data/
**/tools/

.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Thumbs.db
